1
00:00:39,740 --> 00:00:40,617
Thank

2
00:00:40,700 --> 00:00:41,577
you

3
00:00:41,660 --> 00:00:48,660
so

4
00:00:52,320 --> 00:00:53,379
much for watching.

5
00:01:22,340 --> 00:01:24,164
Thank you so much for watching.

6
00:01:36,240 --> 00:01:37,887
Damn it, I don't understand.

7
00:01:46,840 --> 00:01:51,440
But how are you going to kill
what you can't understand?

8
00:01:56,080 --> 00:01:57,220
Paper art.

9
00:01:58,500 --> 00:01:59,720
After image.

10
00:02:03,720 --> 00:02:05,120
My goodness.

11
00:02:07,900 --> 00:02:10,260
You're a wild one, aren't you?

12
00:02:10,960 --> 00:02:12,140
See, prism stone

13
00:02:30,820 --> 00:02:32,173
You backstabbing witch!

14
00:02:34,280 --> 00:02:36,986
I would be a fool to
fight you on even ground.

15
00:02:37,320 --> 00:02:40,420
I know just how strong you are, after all.

16
00:02:42,620 --> 00:02:44,360
I hope you'll forgive me.

17
00:02:49,620 --> 00:02:51,860
What exactly am I seeing right now?

18
00:02:52,340 --> 00:02:54,700
Why are CP-Zero fighting each other?

19
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:57,540
So, why'd you suddenly turn on these guys?

20
00:02:57,700 --> 00:02:58,977
You have a falling out?

21
00:02:59,060 --> 00:03:00,400
This is Stussy here.

22
00:03:00,600 --> 00:03:02,380
I put both of them to sleep.

23
00:03:03,680 --> 00:03:05,520
What happened to CP-Zero?

24
00:03:05,720 --> 00:03:07,080
Tell us something, man!

25
00:03:08,520 --> 00:03:10,760
Seems she even took Lucci by surprise.

26
00:03:13,480 --> 00:03:14,460
Stussy did it.

27
00:03:14,740 --> 00:03:16,916
That's one less thing to worry about.

28
00:03:19,280 --> 00:03:21,200
Mother of gastric distension!

29
00:03:21,640 --> 00:03:23,117
York, say something, York.

30
00:03:23,200 --> 00:03:24,030
Anything!

31
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:26,560
I'm done.

32
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:29,840
I can't eat another bite.

33
00:03:30,040 --> 00:03:31,697
Hey, rise and shine, Back.

34
00:03:31,780 --> 00:03:33,597
We are neck deep in the soup here.

35
00:03:33,680 --> 00:03:35,880
So, who's this Stussy person?

36
00:03:36,080 --> 00:03:37,897
She is a loyal friend who's been working

37
00:03:37,980 --> 00:03:41,657
undercover as a CP0 agent for
over 20 years. Undercover?

38
00:03:41,740 --> 00:03:44,877
That's pretty bold, sending a
spy to an intelligence agency.

39
00:03:44,960 --> 00:03:49,313
It was not part of our original plan,
but that is the way things unfolded.

40
00:03:49,680 --> 00:03:50,860
One issue, Doctor.

41
00:03:51,320 --> 00:03:54,379
I'm afraid my authority
rank is the same as Luchi's.

42
00:03:54,480 --> 00:03:57,080
I can't override his
orders to the Seraphim.

43
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:06,120
In other words, I can't stop them.

44
00:04:08,940 --> 00:04:10,957
Don't worry, Stacy. You did great.

45
00:04:11,040 --> 00:04:13,440
Lilith and I will take it from here.

46
00:04:13,700 --> 00:04:15,465
Let's get our giant kids back.

47
00:04:22,120 --> 00:04:25,037
We gotta stop those weird
things before it's too late.

48
00:04:25,120 --> 00:04:27,637
At this rate, the whole
crew's gonna get buried.

49
00:04:27,720 --> 00:04:28,560
You're right.

50
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:30,212
This is quite troubling.

51
00:04:30,740 --> 00:04:32,800
They look hauntingly familiar.

52
00:04:33,920 --> 00:04:34,920
Yeah, no kidding.

53
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:38,120
Especially... him.

54
00:04:54,480 --> 00:04:57,217
I'm gonna ground them for
a hundred years for this.

55
00:04:57,300 --> 00:04:59,957
Well, at least they made
us a path to the outside.

56
00:05:00,040 --> 00:05:00,870
No, Marcy!

57
00:05:01,460 --> 00:05:02,540
No, Lilith, wait!

58
00:05:02,840 --> 00:05:05,428
Just give them an order
like normal, please!

59
00:05:07,740 --> 00:05:08,780
Okay, freedom.

60
00:05:12,160 --> 00:05:14,200
Hey, Seraphim!

61
00:05:14,620 --> 00:05:16,480
Got an order for you!

62
00:05:55,080 --> 00:05:59,257
guess you're different
after all he's a cold

63
00:05:59,340 --> 00:06:02,281
-blooded killer but he
almost since fear from you.

64
00:06:06,200 --> 00:06:07,280
Out with it.

65
00:06:07,540 --> 00:06:08,640
Who are you?

66
00:06:18,960 --> 00:06:20,980
That really killed me!

67
00:06:21,760 --> 00:06:22,980
Are you okay, Lily?

68
00:06:23,540 --> 00:06:24,370
That's it!

69
00:06:24,453 --> 00:06:25,988
I'm putting an end to this!

70
00:06:27,340 --> 00:06:28,170
Seraphim!

71
00:06:28,253 --> 00:06:30,080
This is in order!

72
00:06:32,140 --> 00:06:34,480
I can't go!

73
00:06:38,940 --> 00:06:39,900
Edison!

74
00:06:49,620 --> 00:06:51,400
Right on time!

75
00:06:51,840 --> 00:06:52,900
You saved me.

76
00:06:54,380 --> 00:06:55,340
Edison!

77
00:06:57,960 --> 00:06:58,790
Oh, no.

78
00:06:59,080 --> 00:07:00,139
Tell me he's okay.

79
00:07:09,100 --> 00:07:11,740
Lilith, darling, don't
fret another moment.

80
00:07:12,440 --> 00:07:13,540
Your thing's safe.

81
00:07:16,380 --> 00:07:18,240
It is so hot!

82
00:07:19,440 --> 00:07:20,680
Holy motility.

83
00:07:21,060 --> 00:07:24,540
Was that a neuropsychiatric
episode or did I see heaven?

84
00:07:39,600 --> 00:07:43,012
I don't know why, but it seems
like they're done fighting.

85
00:07:44,020 --> 00:07:46,820
Hey, you want to tell me
who the hell they are?

86
00:07:47,400 --> 00:07:48,341
Why'd they stop?

87
00:07:49,900 --> 00:07:50,900
Oh, these guys?

88
00:07:51,300 --> 00:07:54,257
They're our sweet little murder
babies, and we're so proud of them.

89
00:07:54,340 --> 00:07:56,677
What she means is they're our cyborgs.

90
00:07:56,760 --> 00:08:00,377
CP0 gave them an order to attack
us, but our authority is higher,

91
00:08:00,460 --> 00:08:03,577
so when we ordered them to stop,
it overrode the previous command.

92
00:08:03,660 --> 00:08:06,300
Oh, what's wrong, Mosshead?

93
00:08:06,480 --> 00:08:10,068
Are you having trouble keeping
up with the rest of the class?

94
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:12,600
Keep up with this, idiot cook!

95
00:08:12,720 --> 00:08:15,217
Zoro, Mets, deactivate
your dumb ass mouth!

96
00:08:15,300 --> 00:08:17,418
Don't talk to me like a damn cyborg!

97
00:08:18,460 --> 00:08:21,637
Well, we survived that mess,
but what's next on the agenda?

98
00:08:21,720 --> 00:08:22,780
What else? Dr.

99
00:08:22,900 --> 00:08:24,917
Vegapunk gave us an
important mission, remember?

100
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:27,397
We're getting him off this island safely,

101
00:08:27,480 --> 00:08:30,340
and we're taking all
his satellites with us!

102
00:08:31,360 --> 00:08:32,190
Aw!

103
00:08:32,273 --> 00:08:33,169
Heck yeah, positive vibes!

104
00:08:34,540 --> 00:08:35,660
Wow! Super!

105
00:08:38,260 --> 00:08:39,090
Shaka.

106
00:08:41,520 --> 00:08:44,680
I put Sea Prism Stone
handcuffs on Luchi and Kaku.

107
00:08:45,380 --> 00:08:47,380
Excellent work, Stussy. Thank you.

108
00:08:47,740 --> 00:08:50,937
We're going to have the Straw Hats
take us off the island on their ship.

109
00:08:51,020 --> 00:08:53,457
I think it would be wise
for you to come with us.

110
00:08:53,540 --> 00:08:54,370
Agreed.

111
00:08:54,800 --> 00:08:58,800
Stop inviting people into our
house! Who raised you? Call it.

112
00:09:01,720 --> 00:09:02,550
Hey!

113
00:09:03,600 --> 00:09:04,430
Bonnie!

114
00:09:04,860 --> 00:09:06,460
Mr. Appleman!

115
00:09:07,100 --> 00:09:08,360
Where'd you go?

116
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:09,830
Wolf!

117
00:09:10,600 --> 00:09:13,000
Hey, Chumper! You find him?

118
00:09:13,620 --> 00:09:15,444
No, it's like they disappeared.

119
00:09:15,800 --> 00:09:16,840
This is weird.

120
00:09:17,160 --> 00:09:18,807
I hope nothing bad happened.

121
00:09:19,200 --> 00:09:20,357
I'll check this way.

122
00:09:20,440 --> 00:09:22,680
Good luck! You too. Thanks!

123
00:09:23,480 --> 00:09:24,740
Man, what a mess.

124
00:09:26,060 --> 00:09:26,890
Hey!

125
00:09:26,973 --> 00:09:27,820
Stop hiding already!

126
00:09:28,240 --> 00:09:30,220
We can't set sail without you!

127
00:09:31,220 --> 00:09:35,867
The Straw Hats encountered Bonnie at sea
and rescued her from a floating alley.

128
00:09:36,040 --> 00:09:38,817
Afterwards, they all traveled
to the future island egghead.

129
00:09:38,900 --> 00:09:42,120
But their plan encountered
an unexpected snag.

130
00:09:43,180 --> 00:09:44,360
Old man!

131
00:09:48,360 --> 00:09:49,190
Dr.

132
00:09:49,273 --> 00:09:52,040
Vegapunk, Stella, disappeared.

133
00:09:55,020 --> 00:09:57,797
This is Sphinx in the New World.

134
00:09:57,880 --> 00:10:01,577
It's the hometown of the
famous pirate Whitebeard.

135
00:10:01,660 --> 00:10:07,897
I was so scared.

136
00:10:07,980 --> 00:10:09,817
I'm so glad you're back, Marco!

137
00:10:09,900 --> 00:10:12,400
I wasn't scared at all, for the record.

138
00:10:12,980 --> 00:10:15,417
The Navy came barging
in here out of nowhere.

139
00:10:15,500 --> 00:10:17,177
I'm sorry, you guys.

140
00:10:17,260 --> 00:10:18,997
That does sound scary!

141
00:10:19,080 --> 00:10:21,917
I wish I'd been here to
protect you from those jerks.

142
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:23,960
Okay, but I said I wasn't scared.

143
00:10:24,200 --> 00:10:26,100
So tell me, what did they do?

144
00:10:26,340 --> 00:10:27,458
All sorts of stuff.

145
00:10:27,600 --> 00:10:29,840
Those marines were horrible! Huh?

146
00:10:30,180 --> 00:10:31,917
They wanted Whitebeard's treasure!

147
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:33,357
They were gonna steal it!

148
00:10:33,440 --> 00:10:35,280
Just like a bunch of pirates!

149
00:10:37,960 --> 00:10:38,790
Huh?

150
00:10:39,120 --> 00:10:39,950
Huh?

151
00:10:44,040 --> 00:10:45,340
What is this?

152
00:11:01,680 --> 00:11:05,400
Drag out the villagers and
gather them all here. Yes, sir!

153
00:11:10,580 --> 00:11:13,980
I won't harm you, as long
as you do what I say.

154
00:11:14,480 --> 00:11:17,997
Which is quite generous of me, since
you're not protected by the law.

155
00:11:18,080 --> 00:11:21,357
And this island's independent
from the world government, right?

156
00:11:21,440 --> 00:11:25,440
I believe Whitebeard's treasure is
hidden somewhere in this country.

157
00:11:25,740 --> 00:11:28,040
Tell me where it is now! Stop this!

158
00:11:28,240 --> 00:11:29,817
We don't know what you're talking about!

159
00:11:29,900 --> 00:11:32,577
This is the first time
I've heard of any treasure!

160
00:11:32,660 --> 00:11:33,580
Oh, well.

161
00:11:35,040 --> 00:11:36,620
That's that, I suppose.

162
00:11:41,040 --> 00:11:41,870
I...

163
00:11:41,953 --> 00:11:42,783
I swear...

164
00:11:42,866 --> 00:11:44,699
You know what I call your defiance!

165
00:11:45,120 --> 00:11:48,061
An act of aggression against
the world government!

166
00:11:48,660 --> 00:11:51,140
So let's do it this way.

167
00:11:53,480 --> 00:11:55,740
I'm going to shoot you one by one.

168
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:57,941
Will you lead me to the treasure?

169
00:11:59,600 --> 00:12:00,430
Stop it!

170
00:12:00,520 --> 00:12:02,108
The treasure doesn't exist!

171
00:12:02,280 --> 00:12:04,537
Please don't point a gun at my brother!

172
00:12:04,620 --> 00:12:08,980
We may not be able to afford our
taxes, but we still are human beings.

173
00:12:09,300 --> 00:12:11,080
Don't treat us like animals!

174
00:12:11,420 --> 00:12:12,500
You're not scared.

175
00:12:12,940 --> 00:12:15,940
I know Marco isn't here
to protect you right now.

176
00:12:17,740 --> 00:12:18,570
Restrain her!

177
00:12:19,320 --> 00:12:21,440
What are you doing? Let me go!

178
00:12:21,940 --> 00:12:23,060
I want help!

179
00:12:23,520 --> 00:12:24,520
You brutes!

180
00:12:24,620 --> 00:12:26,020
Get your hands off me!

181
00:12:27,620 --> 00:12:28,900
Leave her alone!

182
00:12:29,080 --> 00:12:30,217
She's not a threat!

183
00:12:30,300 --> 00:12:31,880
Don't you hurt her!

184
00:12:33,600 --> 00:12:34,640
Stop it!

185
00:12:34,880 --> 00:12:35,920
Let him go!

186
00:13:02,920 --> 00:13:07,840
Don't mess with my daddy's
hometown, or I'll smash you!

187
00:13:09,660 --> 00:13:11,380
It's Edward Weevil!

188
00:13:12,300 --> 00:13:16,040
We gotta get out of here!
Yeah, let's go! Just leave her!

189
00:13:16,860 --> 00:13:18,040
Why is he here?

190
00:13:18,220 --> 00:13:21,637
I thought we sent troops to arrest him
when they shut down the seven warlords!

191
00:13:21,720 --> 00:13:24,097
Yeah, but those troops were
never heard from again!

192
00:13:24,180 --> 00:13:25,010
No way!

193
00:13:25,093 --> 00:13:25,960
He beat them all!

194
00:13:26,200 --> 00:13:27,280
That's no man!

195
00:13:27,460 --> 00:13:28,342
He's a monster!

196
00:13:28,800 --> 00:13:30,317
Retain to the ship for now!

197
00:13:30,400 --> 00:13:32,165
We'll wait for reinforcements!

198
00:13:32,560 --> 00:13:33,390
This is Vince!

199
00:13:33,473 --> 00:13:36,497
We were attacked by the
former warlord Edward Weevil!

200
00:13:36,580 --> 00:13:38,220
We need backup! Hurry!

201
00:13:40,040 --> 00:13:42,180
And then, the Marines went away!

202
00:13:42,360 --> 00:13:44,007
They just waited out at sea!

203
00:13:45,360 --> 00:13:47,657
We're lucky that big guy
showed up when he did.

204
00:13:47,740 --> 00:13:50,269
Because they were really
going to shoot us?

205
00:13:51,040 --> 00:13:52,860
So he saved the day, huh?

206
00:13:53,100 --> 00:13:54,857
I'm really glad everyone made it out safe.

207
00:13:54,940 --> 00:13:56,977
That's not the end of the story, Marco!

208
00:13:57,060 --> 00:13:59,860
Someone else showed up
and ruined everything.

209
00:14:01,480 --> 00:14:03,977
Navy Admiral Ryokugyu.

210
00:14:04,060 --> 00:14:07,317
My precious weevil resisted so bravely.

211
00:14:07,400 --> 00:14:09,020
But that rat took him away.

212
00:14:10,180 --> 00:14:11,010
Weevil!

213
00:14:11,280 --> 00:14:12,110
Mommy!

214
00:14:15,200 --> 00:14:18,100
You're going to help me
get my son back! My son!

215
00:14:19,380 --> 00:14:20,600
And my treasure!

216
00:14:20,900 --> 00:14:22,937
Edward Newgate's inheritance will be mine!

217
00:14:23,020 --> 00:14:23,850
You hear me?

218
00:14:24,280 --> 00:14:25,110
Mine!

219
00:14:30,060 --> 00:14:30,890
No,

220
00:14:30,973 --> 00:14:33,517
I'm just worried sick
about my sweet boy who

221
00:14:33,600 --> 00:14:36,365
sacrificed his freedom
for his daddy's village!

222
00:14:36,660 --> 00:14:39,580
Oh, Newgate, what have
they done to our baby?

223
00:14:42,380 --> 00:14:44,460
At any rate, I guess I owe him one.

224
00:14:44,740 --> 00:14:46,916
I'm glad he was here for the village.

225
00:14:48,420 --> 00:14:49,960
I know that tone.

226
00:14:50,280 --> 00:14:51,817
You're just like all the others.

227
00:14:51,900 --> 00:14:55,312
You don't believe Weevil is
Whitebeard's real son, do you?

228
00:14:55,600 --> 00:14:57,835
Well, I know someone who can prove it.

229
00:14:59,740 --> 00:15:00,570
Dr.

230
00:15:00,653 --> 00:15:01,808
Vegapunk will show you all.

231
00:15:11,640 --> 00:15:15,405
Admiral, we brought tea cakes for
your meeting as you requested.

232
00:15:15,700 --> 00:15:18,288
Ah, you've tested them
for poison, I assume?

233
00:15:18,460 --> 00:15:19,290
Of course.

234
00:15:19,580 --> 00:15:22,500
I'll take it from here. At ease, kid. Sir!

235
00:15:35,980 --> 00:15:37,340
Pardon the intrusion.

236
00:15:38,880 --> 00:15:41,397
I thought you could use some refreshments?

237
00:15:41,480 --> 00:15:44,060
Allow me to serve you.

238
00:15:50,860 --> 00:15:52,717
I've been meaning to ask you.

239
00:15:52,800 --> 00:15:54,920
Have you ever met Dr.

240
00:15:55,040 --> 00:15:55,981
Vegapunk before?

241
00:15:56,940 --> 00:15:58,140
I have

242
00:16:03,420 --> 00:16:09,380
Just once A long time ago It's hard
to believe that he betrayed you.

243
00:16:09,880 --> 00:16:12,200
Not a bright move for a genius.

244
00:16:23,160 --> 00:16:28,180
Yes, I must say, this is quite
the regrettable turn of events.

245
00:16:31,280 --> 00:16:32,580
It can't be!

246
00:16:43,260 --> 00:16:44,300
Oh, Pacifista!

247
00:16:44,680 --> 00:16:45,857
What's wrong with it?

248
00:16:45,940 --> 00:16:47,140
Hey, stop it!

249
00:16:47,320 --> 00:16:49,077
You're attacking the wrong guys!

250
00:16:49,160 --> 00:16:50,925
We're with the government too!

251
00:16:51,540 --> 00:16:53,520
Hey, did you hear what I said?

252
00:17:06,120 --> 00:17:07,860
Die, you monster!

253
00:17:11,540 --> 00:17:13,340
Wait! Don't shoot!

254
00:17:30,120 --> 00:17:31,826
What the hell did he just do?

255
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:34,060
It looked like a bubble shield.

256
00:17:34,280 --> 00:17:36,777
They say that's one of
Vegapunk's greatest inventions.

257
00:17:36,860 --> 00:17:38,617
It has the power to repel anything.

258
00:17:38,700 --> 00:17:39,530
Damn it.

259
00:17:39,613 --> 00:17:41,297
It's nothing like the ones in Marineford.

260
00:17:41,380 --> 00:17:42,557
It's a brand new model.

261
00:17:42,640 --> 00:17:44,440
The Pacifista Mark III.

262
00:17:56,980 --> 00:17:59,820
Submit and relocate to Factory B.

263
00:18:03,480 --> 00:18:05,660
Hostile activity confirmed.

264
00:18:08,380 --> 00:18:10,100
We're all gonna die!

265
00:18:10,320 --> 00:18:11,438
Please don't shoot!

266
00:18:11,660 --> 00:18:12,640
We surrender!

267
00:18:19,760 --> 00:18:21,680
You are under arrest.

268
00:18:25,820 --> 00:18:26,957
Please just wait.

269
00:18:27,040 --> 00:18:29,257
Pacifistas never make
decisions on their own.

270
00:18:29,340 --> 00:18:31,420
Who's giving you these orders?

271
00:18:37,820 --> 00:18:38,977
Please don't move.

272
00:18:39,060 --> 00:18:40,520
You'll open your wounds.

273
00:18:43,080 --> 00:18:45,317
And this was supposed to be my day off.

274
00:18:45,400 --> 00:18:46,817
How is the pacifista?

275
00:18:46,900 --> 00:18:48,400
Is it doing its job?

276
00:18:51,220 --> 00:18:53,177
Something bad is happening up there.

277
00:18:53,260 --> 00:18:55,900
Punk, do you copy? It's me.

278
00:18:57,800 --> 00:18:59,660
Punk, say something!

279
00:19:01,560 --> 00:19:02,957
He can't hear me.

280
00:19:03,040 --> 00:19:04,517
The dome is closed.

281
00:19:04,600 --> 00:19:05,430
We're shut out.

282
00:19:05,513 --> 00:19:07,097
I'm sorry, Punk.

283
00:19:07,180 --> 00:19:08,797
I can't protect you.

284
00:19:08,880 --> 00:19:11,277
Go and take care of Punk.

285
00:19:11,360 --> 00:19:12,520
You hear me?

286
00:19:13,680 --> 00:19:15,680
Okay, leave it to me

287
00:19:18,920 --> 00:19:23,237
The Navy hasn't stopped communication,
but they've cut us out of the loop.

288
00:19:23,320 --> 00:19:25,379
Guess that tells us where we stand.

289
00:19:28,660 --> 00:19:32,260
In the world's eyes,
I'm already a traitor.

290
00:19:36,080 --> 00:19:38,280
Might as well do as I please, then.

291
00:19:39,900 --> 00:19:42,100
Pacifista, mark three, activate!

292
00:19:52,440 --> 00:19:54,860
All 50 units, dispatch!

293
00:19:58,980 --> 00:20:01,360
Straw Hat Luffy is going to take Dr.

294
00:20:01,480 --> 00:20:03,817
Vegapunk off the island aboard his ship.

295
00:20:03,900 --> 00:20:06,720
Your mission is to make
sure it departs safely.

296
00:20:07,340 --> 00:20:08,170
Understood.

297
00:20:12,620 --> 00:20:14,600
The Navy is up to something.

298
00:20:15,460 --> 00:20:19,240
Keep an eye on the shore,
something big is about to happen.

299
00:20:20,660 --> 00:20:21,490
Dr.

300
00:20:21,573 --> 00:20:27,360
Vegapunk is your creator, protect him,
no matter what, get him off this island.

301
00:20:30,720 --> 00:20:33,540
Bonnie, please, I'm begging you.

302
00:20:33,780 --> 00:20:35,486
I've heard enough out of you.

303
00:20:37,580 --> 00:20:38,410
Bonnie!

304
00:21:00,240 --> 00:21:03,060
Oh, my God.

305
00:21:34,780 --> 00:21:36,040
Are you all right?

306
00:21:36,320 --> 00:21:38,760
Hey, what happened to you?

307
00:21:41,580 --> 00:21:42,680
It's over.

308
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:44,440
I tried, but...

309
00:21:44,600 --> 00:21:46,520
I just can't...

310
00:21:48,740 --> 00:21:50,720
Is that you? Dad?

311
00:22:01,600 --> 00:22:02,977
Thought you could run, boy?

312
00:22:03,060 --> 00:22:05,240
Get on your damn feet! Now!

313
00:22:06,300 --> 00:22:07,880
No, please! Go away!

314
00:22:08,340 --> 00:22:09,399
Stop your whining!

315
00:22:09,620 --> 00:22:12,000
You're coming with us! Come here!

316
00:22:15,460 --> 00:22:21,620
No, I'm begging you, let me go,
let me go, someone help me please,

317
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:22,880
help me!

318
00:22:22,980 --> 00:22:25,440
Stop squirming, move it, come on!

319
00:22:25,720 --> 00:22:27,200
We're not letting you go!

320
00:22:27,460 --> 00:22:29,937
If you escape, they're
gonna execute us all!

321
00:22:30,020 --> 00:22:34,220
But I, I can't, I don't wanna go
back, I don't wanna go back there!

322
00:22:35,460 --> 00:22:37,597
Help me, please go away!

323
00:22:37,680 --> 00:22:38,974
Search your damn boat!

324
00:22:39,680 --> 00:22:40,677
Somebody help!

325
00:22:40,760 --> 00:22:41,660
Help!

326
00:22:43,320 --> 00:22:45,220
Let him go!

327
00:22:45,980 --> 00:22:47,100
Just please me!

328
00:22:47,300 --> 00:22:49,140
Please don't make me go fast!

329
00:22:51,760 --> 00:22:52,590
Stop it!

330
00:22:52,673 --> 00:22:54,228
He said he doesn't want to!

331
00:22:58,360 --> 00:23:00,260
Wait, what's happening?

332
00:23:01,760 --> 00:23:03,113
Why can't I get closer?

333
00:23:07,760 --> 00:23:10,060
Stop your crying, you little shit.

334
00:23:12,900 --> 00:23:15,280
I can't take it anymore.

335
00:23:15,540 --> 00:23:17,100
I'd rather die!

336
00:23:17,680 --> 00:23:18,510
You're strong!

337
00:23:18,593 --> 00:23:19,423
Come here! No!

338
00:23:20,280 --> 00:23:21,940
I'll never go back!

339
00:23:22,160 --> 00:23:23,984
You might as well just kill me!

340
00:23:24,220 --> 00:23:27,660
If I go back, I'll end up dead anyway!

341
00:23:29,340 --> 00:23:30,170
What?

342
00:23:30,480 --> 00:23:31,640
Shut up, kid!

343
00:23:34,960 --> 00:23:35,790
Stop it!

344
00:23:36,640 --> 00:23:37,470
No!

345
00:23:41,160 --> 00:23:42,240
No!

346
00:23:51,400 --> 00:23:53,560
Come on!

347
00:23:54,020 --> 00:23:54,860
Stop it!

348
00:23:55,080 --> 00:23:56,420
You monsters!

349
00:23:57,460 --> 00:23:59,020
I said stop!

350
00:24:03,360 --> 00:24:04,980
It hurts!

351
00:24:06,140 --> 00:24:08,560
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

352
00:24:08,760 --> 00:24:09,620
I'm sorry!

353
00:24:12,580 --> 00:24:14,760
That's enough! Let him go!

354
00:24:28,460 --> 00:24:31,120
I can't watch this anymore!

355
00:24:33,460 --> 00:24:35,180
I can't take it!

356
00:24:35,400 --> 00:24:37,020
Someone help me!

357
00:24:37,620 --> 00:24:38,480
No more!

358
00:24:39,080 --> 00:24:39,910
No more!

359
00:24:39,993 --> 00:24:41,160
Please, no more!

360
00:24:41,860 --> 00:24:43,940
Stop hurting him!

361
00:25:01,800 --> 00:25:03,560
Shoot him down!

362
00:25:13,660 --> 00:25:16,397
Bartholomew Kuma is continuing
to climb the Red Line!

363
00:25:16,480 --> 00:25:18,617
He appears to be heading for Paris-Joyal!

364
00:25:18,700 --> 00:25:21,877
Do not let him enter the Holy
Land, no matter the cost!

365
00:25:21,960 --> 00:25:24,080
The Navy's reputation is at stake!

366
00:25:24,400 --> 00:25:26,100
This is our swore duty!

367
00:25:33,760 --> 00:25:35,240
My father's past.

368
00:25:36,240 --> 00:25:38,200
I don't know if I can face it.

369
00:25:40,380 --> 00:25:42,817
I don't know if I have the strength,

370
00:25:42,900 --> 00:25:47,600
but I have to.

371
00:25:50,020 --> 00:25:52,300
I need to find out the truth.

372
00:25:54,640 --> 00:25:55,470
Okay.

373
00:25:55,940 --> 00:25:57,080
I'm ready, Dad.

374
00:26:01,200 --> 00:26:02,460
Kill me again.

375
00:26:03,000 --> 00:26:03,960
I'll stay.

376
00:26:11,200 --> 00:26:13,357
What do you mean you
couldn't find Vegapunk?

377
00:26:13,440 --> 00:26:15,457
There are only so many places he could be!

378
00:26:15,540 --> 00:26:18,077
Maybe there's some secret
passage where you didn't see?

379
00:26:18,160 --> 00:26:18,990
There must be!

380
00:26:22,860 --> 00:26:24,160
No, he's gone.

381
00:26:24,820 --> 00:26:27,500
I ran everywhere looking for the guy.

382
00:26:29,780 --> 00:26:32,300
And now I'm dying and he's still lost.

383
00:26:32,500 --> 00:26:33,676
Oh, come on, really?

384
00:26:33,800 --> 00:26:34,700
Yes, really!

385
00:26:34,960 --> 00:26:37,157
The hover function on his
shoes stopped working.

386
00:26:37,240 --> 00:26:38,397
I think he broke them!

387
00:26:38,480 --> 00:26:41,517
Don't tell people that they're
gonna make me pay for new ones.

388
00:26:41,600 --> 00:26:44,557
Nobody cares about the damn
shoes We're all about to die.

389
00:26:44,640 --> 00:26:46,777
If he's not in the lab, then
where could he have gone?

390
00:26:46,860 --> 00:26:48,100
Just chill out a sec,

391
00:26:48,200 --> 00:26:51,377
Usopp We don't have a sec if we
don't leave now They're gonna

392
00:26:51,460 --> 00:26:54,377
sit a whole fleet of those
suit-wearing sadists after us.

393
00:26:54,460 --> 00:26:56,989
We know but we can't
leave without Vegapunk

394
00:26:57,700 --> 00:26:59,877
What the heck are you trying to pull Mr.

395
00:26:59,960 --> 00:27:00,790
Appleman?

396
00:27:00,900 --> 00:27:02,135
Bonnie's missing too.

397
00:27:02,440 --> 00:27:04,264
Maybe she's calmed down by now.

398
00:27:04,380 --> 00:27:05,580
I know where she is

399
00:27:06,160 --> 00:27:06,990
Huh?

400
00:27:07,220 --> 00:27:09,573
I can see her right here on the monitor.

401
00:27:09,700 --> 00:27:10,876
Wait, you found her?

402
00:27:10,960 --> 00:27:11,797
Never lost her.

403
00:27:11,880 --> 00:27:12,762
Never lost her!

404
00:27:14,900 --> 00:27:15,730
Hey!

405
00:27:15,813 --> 00:27:16,740
What a mess.

406
00:27:18,000 --> 00:27:18,830
Zoro!

407
00:27:18,913 --> 00:27:20,624
I thought we were setting sail.

408
00:27:20,720 --> 00:27:22,757
What are you doing just
sitting around in here?

409
00:27:22,840 --> 00:27:24,657
Well, he kind of had some issues.

410
00:27:24,740 --> 00:27:27,537
Well, I wouldn't blame you for
wanting to tilly-tally a bit.

411
00:27:27,620 --> 00:27:29,620
Just look, it's all so futuristic.

412
00:27:30,160 --> 00:27:31,680
Wow, I'll say!

413
00:27:31,940 --> 00:27:34,637
They even invented a high-tech
hat that shows off your eyebrows!

414
00:27:34,720 --> 00:27:37,560
A fishbowl is your idea
of high-tech, really?

415
00:27:38,200 --> 00:27:39,580
This is quite a wreck.

416
00:27:41,980 --> 00:27:44,340
Shaka, who's Atlas doing? Let me see.

417
00:27:44,720 --> 00:27:46,540
Edison, Lilith, status report.

418
00:27:46,800 --> 00:27:47,700
The statuses?

419
00:27:47,840 --> 00:27:48,800
You still suck!

420
00:27:48,980 --> 00:27:49,817
Move, Lilith.

421
00:27:49,900 --> 00:27:52,317
I just finished the
repairs on Atlas, Shaka.

422
00:27:52,400 --> 00:27:53,230
Come see.

423
00:27:53,313 --> 00:27:55,612
We, plural, we just finished the repairs.

424
00:27:55,820 --> 00:27:58,173
I worked on her just as much as you did.

425
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:01,040
Hey, gang!

426
00:28:01,360 --> 00:28:02,237
Guess who's back?

427
00:28:02,320 --> 00:28:03,920
She's got dance! Hit me up!

428
00:28:04,140 --> 00:28:05,140
It's human kicks!

429
00:28:07,700 --> 00:28:09,580
Human Atlas! Oh, no!

430
00:28:11,380 --> 00:28:13,300
Matt, look! I'm alive!

431
00:28:13,540 --> 00:28:14,880
Yes, I can see that!

432
00:28:15,180 --> 00:28:17,121
Gosh, she sure is full of energy.

433
00:28:17,320 --> 00:28:18,849
I guess we did a good job.

434
00:28:24,840 --> 00:28:27,340
Hey, girl, hey, looking good. Thanks!

435
00:28:27,640 --> 00:28:29,111
Did you just wake up now?

436
00:28:29,200 --> 00:28:30,397
You kind of missed a lot.

437
00:28:30,480 --> 00:28:33,656
If you want, I'll smack the
drowsies right out of you!

438
00:28:34,240 --> 00:28:36,534
How about you don't and say you didn't?

439
00:28:39,000 --> 00:28:39,860
Oh, good.

440
00:28:40,080 --> 00:28:41,697
I'm glad her face got better.

441
00:28:41,780 --> 00:28:43,662
We had replacement lights ready.

442
00:28:45,020 --> 00:28:46,060
Hey, it's you!

443
00:28:46,240 --> 00:28:48,297
You're the little guy who saved my bacon!

444
00:28:48,380 --> 00:28:49,537
Thanks a bunch, bud!

445
00:28:49,620 --> 00:28:50,450
No problem!

446
00:28:51,560 --> 00:28:54,317
So you've started being
up little girls now, huh?

447
00:28:54,400 --> 00:28:57,737
You creeps are every bit as rotten
as you were when we first met you!

448
00:28:57,820 --> 00:29:02,232
If you so much as look at Robin again,
I'll put you straight in the ground!

449
00:29:03,520 --> 00:29:06,108
Nami, there's nothing
they can do to me now.

450
00:29:06,420 --> 00:29:10,361
That said, I wanted to see Stella,
but it seems something happened.

451
00:29:11,200 --> 00:29:14,847
Unfortunately, we've been faced
with two unpleasant surprises.

452
00:29:15,500 --> 00:29:17,280
First, Stella has disappeared.

453
00:29:18,000 --> 00:29:20,824
Second, we've lost control
of the Frontier Dome.

454
00:29:22,700 --> 00:29:24,524
And what does that mean for us?

455
00:29:25,300 --> 00:29:30,120
It means for the time being we're trapped
inside the level phase with no escape.

456
00:29:31,540 --> 00:29:34,057
If anyone tries to leave laser beams will

457
00:29:34,140 --> 00:29:36,877
incinerate them immediately
are you kidding me?

458
00:29:36,960 --> 00:29:38,997
We're supposed to take
Vegapunk to sea like

459
00:29:39,080 --> 00:29:42,157
urgently aren't we ideally
but we can't do that.

460
00:29:42,240 --> 00:29:45,117
While he's missing what
are we supposed to do

461
00:29:45,200 --> 00:29:48,560
let me handle the dome
you go look for stella.

462
00:29:49,280 --> 00:29:51,633
That's the only solution afforded to us.

463
00:29:51,900 --> 00:29:52,782
Quick question.

464
00:29:53,160 --> 00:29:56,877
You got monitors that show the whole lab,
but you said you can't see Vegapunk on it.

465
00:29:56,960 --> 00:29:59,377
So what's the point in
a search of the place?

466
00:29:59,460 --> 00:30:02,695
Normally, we can see everything,
but not at the moment.

467
00:30:03,160 --> 00:30:06,177
The Seraphim's Rampage did
quite a number on this place.

468
00:30:06,260 --> 00:30:09,495
Many of the Camp Snells are
either lost or unconscious.

469
00:30:10,280 --> 00:30:13,104
We need everyone to check
the unsurveiled areas.

470
00:30:13,960 --> 00:30:17,901
Stella could be incapacitated in
one of the Camp Snell blind spots.

471
00:30:18,360 --> 00:30:20,037
Shaka, this is Pythagoras.

472
00:30:20,120 --> 00:30:22,137
I'm on the third floor of building C.

473
00:30:22,220 --> 00:30:23,337
And it's crickets up here.

474
00:30:23,420 --> 00:30:24,317
I see.

475
00:30:24,400 --> 00:30:26,877
Then check the next building
over while you're there.

476
00:30:26,960 --> 00:30:28,717
We should start looking too.

477
00:30:28,800 --> 00:30:31,297
The sooner we get out of
here, the better after all.

478
00:30:31,380 --> 00:30:34,457
And I might find some future
treasure along the way.

479
00:30:34,540 --> 00:30:36,057
That sounds delightful.

480
00:30:36,140 --> 00:30:37,397
I think I'll come too.

481
00:30:37,480 --> 00:30:39,317
Hey, I don't like the sound of that.

482
00:30:39,400 --> 00:30:41,497
You guys aren't going to
start any trouble, are you?

483
00:30:41,580 --> 00:30:43,860
We would never, right, Amu?

484
00:30:44,000 --> 00:30:45,057
Yeah, let's go with that.

485
00:30:45,140 --> 00:30:46,457
That wasn't convincing at all!

486
00:30:46,540 --> 00:30:47,837
Stay where I can see you.

487
00:30:47,920 --> 00:30:49,797
If you don't mind, I'll search as well.

488
00:30:49,880 --> 00:30:51,917
It's not like him to disappear like this.

489
00:30:52,000 --> 00:30:53,637
Mind if I come along with you?

490
00:30:53,720 --> 00:30:55,160
Of course. I'm grateful.

491
00:30:56,380 --> 00:30:58,380
Susie, let me come too, please.

492
00:30:58,640 --> 00:31:00,977
I'll follow you to the ends of the earth.

493
00:31:01,060 --> 00:31:01,890
All right.

494
00:31:02,400 --> 00:31:03,860
Guess I'd better go too.

495
00:31:04,200 --> 00:31:06,380
Hold up, Mosshead. What's your deal?

496
00:31:06,560 --> 00:31:08,557
I'm looking for some apple guy, right?

497
00:31:08,640 --> 00:31:09,470
Easy.

498
00:31:09,553 --> 00:31:10,383
Not for you.

499
00:31:10,466 --> 00:31:11,320
No way.

500
00:31:12,040 --> 00:31:13,000
Absolutely not.

501
00:31:13,160 --> 00:31:14,177
I'll knock it off.

502
00:31:14,260 --> 00:31:15,337
What the hell's your problem?

503
00:31:15,420 --> 00:31:18,757
If you're out searching, I know
who's going to search for you!

504
00:31:18,840 --> 00:31:20,760
Come on, man. He's right!

505
00:31:21,100 --> 00:31:24,260
Zoro, please don't go!
You too? No, really.

506
00:31:24,460 --> 00:31:26,107
Be a good boy and stay here.

507
00:31:26,400 --> 00:31:27,230
Whatever.

508
00:31:27,560 --> 00:31:29,560
Let's get our search on, my bros!

509
00:31:29,700 --> 00:31:31,340
I won't let Vega pump down!

510
00:31:31,480 --> 00:31:33,037
But he's like a mate out there!

511
00:31:33,120 --> 00:31:35,137
I've got a really bad feeling about this.

512
00:31:35,220 --> 00:31:37,757
Even if we're not Zoro,
we still might get lost.

513
00:31:37,840 --> 00:31:40,217
How did you guys ever
make it out of a port?

514
00:31:40,300 --> 00:31:42,880
Just follow me! Really? Thanks!

515
00:31:44,100 --> 00:31:45,637
York, are you asleep again?

516
00:31:45,720 --> 00:31:46,550
We need help.

517
00:31:46,633 --> 00:31:48,117
You can nap once we're on the ship.

518
00:31:48,200 --> 00:31:49,030
Yeah!

519
00:31:51,920 --> 00:31:52,750
Okay.

520
00:31:57,480 --> 00:32:01,951
Don't know why they wanted me to stick
around so bad, but I guess it's fine.

521
00:32:02,760 --> 00:32:06,054
I'm sure finding one old man
won't be too hard for them.

522
00:32:06,300 --> 00:32:08,594
But damn, you really went all out, huh?

523
00:32:09,280 --> 00:32:13,420
Ugh, I always go all out.

524
00:32:13,880 --> 00:32:14,939
Yeah, fair enough.

525
00:32:15,680 --> 00:32:18,798
Anyway, I never thought I'd
see these assholes again.

526
00:32:19,100 --> 00:32:20,520
Really takes me back.

527
00:32:20,780 --> 00:32:21,880
Remember Water 7?

528
00:32:22,260 --> 00:32:23,460
Ice Pop's place.

529
00:32:23,720 --> 00:32:25,132
I wonder how he's doing.

530
00:32:31,860 --> 00:32:34,920
Now there's a scoop if I ever heard one!

531
00:32:35,240 --> 00:32:36,737
Who would've thunk?

532
00:32:36,820 --> 00:32:40,349
the government power-drunk, and
they're coming for Vegapunk!

533
00:32:40,660 --> 00:32:43,437
Gunning for the greatest
minds in the world again.

534
00:32:43,520 --> 00:32:46,417
Seems Ohadda was a big
enough hit to get a sequel.

535
00:32:46,500 --> 00:32:48,912
But they'll be hard-pressed to spin this!

536
00:32:49,160 --> 00:32:51,395
Vegapunk's a hero all across the seas!

537
00:32:51,500 --> 00:32:53,577
He brought life to towns all around!

538
00:32:53,660 --> 00:32:56,013
His energy tech made him a shining star!

539
00:32:56,460 --> 00:32:59,780
But he's sharing a stage
on Egghead with him!

540
00:33:01,020 --> 00:33:02,440
Fire up the presses!

541
00:33:03,000 --> 00:33:06,737
The World Economic Journal's got a
scorching hot new front page story!

542
00:33:06,820 --> 00:33:08,200
And the headline is,

543
00:33:08,400 --> 00:33:13,500
Emperor of the Sea Straw Hat Luffy wages
war with the Navy on Egghead and holds Dr.

544
00:33:13,660 --> 00:33:14,700
Vegapunk hostage.

545
00:33:15,160 --> 00:33:17,748
No better villain than
a pirate, am I right?

546
00:33:17,920 --> 00:33:22,177
Now, when the government kills Vegapunk,
they won't get any bad publicity.

547
00:33:22,260 --> 00:33:25,237
And they'll be grateful for
my impeccable journalism.

548
00:33:25,320 --> 00:33:27,077
Remind them we take donations.

549
00:33:27,160 --> 00:33:27,990
Yes, sir.

550
00:33:30,060 --> 00:33:31,640
You're not a journalist.

551
00:33:34,120 --> 00:33:36,340
You're just spinning ridiculous lies.

552
00:33:36,820 --> 00:33:39,017
Luffy would never do
such a horrible thing.

553
00:33:39,100 --> 00:33:41,057
You and the government are pathetic.

554
00:33:41,140 --> 00:33:41,970
Phoebe!

555
00:33:42,053 --> 00:33:43,997
Keep your voice down, are you crazy?

556
00:33:44,080 --> 00:33:46,757
The government could be listening
to our every word right now.

557
00:33:46,840 --> 00:33:48,757
What if they got the whole place bugged?

558
00:33:48,840 --> 00:33:51,840
They're gonna squash us
like bugs! Don't dip it!

559
00:33:51,940 --> 00:33:54,217
And don't forget Morgia's
saving our asses.

560
00:33:54,300 --> 00:33:55,829
Get off his tail feathers!

561
00:33:55,940 --> 00:33:56,822
Absolutely not.

562
00:33:57,020 --> 00:33:58,817
I will not be silent about this.

563
00:33:58,900 --> 00:34:01,597
What gives you the right to twist
the truth for your own gain?

564
00:34:01,680 --> 00:34:03,386
Have you no sense of decency?

565
00:34:04,800 --> 00:34:06,737
Those are my clothes
she's wearing, you know?

566
00:34:06,820 --> 00:34:08,657
And I'll never watch them again!

567
00:34:08,740 --> 00:34:10,200
You're so lucky!

568
00:34:10,520 --> 00:34:11,800
Princess Phoebe!

569
00:34:13,540 --> 00:34:16,397
You were crying your eyes
out yesterday, little girl!

570
00:34:16,480 --> 00:34:20,077
And today you're all high and
mighty telling me how to do my job!

571
00:34:20,160 --> 00:34:21,860
I'm a mover and a shaker!

572
00:34:22,060 --> 00:34:23,460
A big news maker!

573
00:34:23,740 --> 00:34:24,580
Who are you?

574
00:34:25,520 --> 00:34:27,226
Newspapers are entertainment!

575
00:34:27,400 --> 00:34:31,040
So I don't care if they're true or not!

576
00:34:37,680 --> 00:34:42,140
Do you know what's going on?

577
00:35:30,280 --> 00:35:32,600
I'll see you soon.

578
00:35:36,820 --> 00:35:39,820
I'll be laughing at you.

579
00:35:40,400 --> 00:35:44,317
I'll be the same song.

580
00:35:44,400 --> 00:35:46,340
I'll be the same song.

581
00:35:47,400 --> 00:35:48,997
If you're a big man!

582
00:35:49,080 --> 00:35:52,460
I won't forget.

583
00:35:53,980 --> 00:35:56,117
I'll be the same song.

584
00:35:56,200 --> 00:35:58,037
I'll be the

585
00:35:58,120 --> 00:36:04,897
same

586
00:36:04,980 --> 00:36:06,737
song.

587
00:36:06,820 --> 00:36:07,840
Thank you.
